 coords 0 0 0
 m_bRespawnEnabled 0
 m_bWaveRespawn 0
 m_bRallyPointsEnabled 0
 m_iTimeToRespawn 60
 m_iRespawnCutoffMinutes 0
 m_eRespawnMode 0
 m_iTimeLimitMinutes 65
 m_bLockUnusedSlots 1
 m_bUseSafestartTimeLimit 1
 m_iSafestartTimeLimit 15
 m_bUseCVON 1
 m_aMissionDescriptors {
  COA_MissionDescriptor "{6B1109E1A503377C}" {
   m_sTitle "Mission: Situation"
   m_sTextData "Kolguyev, east coast, 0700. Overcast, calm sea."\
   ""\
   "The beach between Gorshkovo and the naval harbour is the only stretch of open shore on this coast. The Germans have turned it into a strongpoint: a belt of hedgehogs in the shallows and more on the sand, two belts of wire up the slope, a line of Tobruk MG pits, two casemates and two hill bunkers above them, and MG nests covering the south draw and the harbour road. Behind the beach the ground climbs past the mining village of Gorshkovo and its coal silo to the Nadezhda coal mine on the ridge, 1.2 km inland and 200 m up."\
   ""\
   "US infantry are loading into LCVPs at a staging pontoon 850 m offshore."\
   ""\
   "BLUFOR: US Army rifle platoon (1PLT, 1-1 to 1-4, WPNS); the weapons squad has the platoon's engineers. A 105 mm M2A1 howitzer section (ARTY) fires from its own pontoon south of the staging pontoon. Eight LCVPs."\
   "OPFOR: German infantry platoon, 1944 (ZUG, GRUPPE 1-3, MG-TRUPP). Dug in, no vehicles."
   m_aFactionKeys {
   }
   m_bShowForAnyFaction 1
  }
  COA_MissionDescriptor "{6B1109E1F61769E7}" {
   m_sTitle "BLUFOR Briefing"
   m_sTextData "MISSION"\
   "Three objectives, one after another (the task list shows the open one and its progress):"\
   "1. Breach the sea wall and control Red Beach."\
   "2. Capture the spotting position at the coal silo."\
   "3. Capture the garrison (Nadezhda mine)."\
   ""\
   "1. RED BEACH"\
   "A concrete sea wall runs along the top of the sand, too high to climb. Six sections of it are breach points (marked on your map): an engineer with a satchel, an M112 block or a Bangalore uses \"Place breaching charge\" on the seaward side of one. The charge is used up and the section blows 10 seconds later - get clear. One breach is enough. Then hold Red Beach (the beach and the slope up to the casemates): at least 3 of you, at most 2 Germans, for 60 seconds."\
   "2. COAL SILO"\
   "The German artillery spotters sit in the tower and the observation post on the silo pad above Gorshkovo. At least 2 of you, at most 1 German, for 45 seconds."\
   "3. NADEZHDA MINE"\
   "The garrison holds the mine yard on the ridge, 1.2 km inland and 200 m up: three huts, tents and the flag. At least 3 of you, at most 1 German, for 90 seconds."\
   "If nobody is there to hold a zone, its progress drains; contested, it holds."\
   ""\
   "EXECUTION"\
   "Each element spawns on the pontoon next to its own LCVP: step down into the boat, the squad lead or a volunteer drives. A belt of hedgehogs lies in the shallows off BEACH RED: come in through one of the three cleared lanes (LANE 1-3 on the map) or the boat hangs up short of the beach. A breach point sits at the head of every lane and between the lanes. The lower wire belt behind the wall has gaps straight up from each lane, the upper belt has gaps between them. Two spare LCVPs wait at the north end of the dock."\
   "After safe start the run in takes about two minutes. Mind the rock awash 130 m off the middle of the beach."\
   ""\
   "ENGINEERS (WPNS): four combat engineers, each with a Bangalore torpedo, three satchel charges, an M112 block and a blasting machine - every one of them can blow a breach point. Spare charges go under the wire: lay a Bangalore and \"Push Bangalore\" to add the next engineer's section."\
   "HOWITZER (ARTY): a 105 mm M2A1 on its own pontoon (HOWITZER on the map), 75 m south of the staging pontoon, laid towards the beach. Two crates next to the gun hold 60 HE (M1) and 100 white phosphorus smoke (M60) rounds - that is all there is. Take a shell from a crate, set its charge, load it into the gun. The section chief and the gunner carry the firing table. The beach is about 1 km away, the silo 1.4 km, the mine 2 km. A dead gun crew respawns with everyone else, at BLUFOR's current spawn."\
   ""\
   "No timed respawns: when an objective falls, everyone dead comes back - after the beach at the beachhead behind the wall, after the silo on the road below it."\
   ""\
   "CASUALTIES: the platoon can take as many casualties as it has men when safe start ends. Every death counts, again after a respawn. Reach that and the Germans win (the pause menu shows the count)."
   m_aFactionKeys {
    "BLUFOR"
   }
   m_bShowForAnyFaction 0
  }
  COA_MissionDescriptor "{6B1109E199D38E4F}" {
   m_sTitle "OPFOR Briefing"
   m_sTextData "MISSION"\
   "Hold three positions, one after another: the sea wall and Red Beach, the artillery spotting position at the coal silo, the garrison at the Nadezhda mine."\
   ""\
   "EXECUTION"\
   "You start on the slope above the beach. Beach Red is fortified: the sea wall along the top of the sand, sandbag bunkers on the beach, four Tobruk MG pits behind the upper wire, two casemates (ladder to the roof) and two hill bunkers above them, MG nests at the south draw and on the harbour road. The boats can only get through three lanes in the hedgehog belt."\
   "The Americans have to blow a gap in the wall first: you are warned when a breaching charge is set (10 s). After that they take the beach if they hold it for 60 seconds with 2 or fewer of you on it."\
   "When a position falls, everyone dead comes back at the next one: the hill west of Gorshkovo for the silo, the road behind the mine for the garrison."\
   "You have no vehicles. Each Gruppe has an MG34 and a Panzerfaust (one shot: save it for a boat), and its grenadier has rifle grenades. The MG-Trupp has two MG42s. Your only medic is the Zug's Sanitäter."\
   ""\
   "YOU WIN if the Americans have not taken all three when the time limit (60 minutes) runs out, if they are wiped out, or if they take as many casualties as they had men when safe start ended (every death counts, again after a respawn; the pause menu shows the count)."
   m_aFactionKeys {
    "OPFOR"
   }
   m_bShowForAnyFaction 0
  }
  COA_MissionDescriptor "{6B1109E10A6C267B}" {
   m_sTitle "Administration"
   m_sTextData "Objective chain, 3 objectives. Time limit 75 minutes after safe start (safe start max. 15 minutes)."\
   ""\
   "No timed respawns. When an objective falls, every dead player of both sides respawns at their side's new spawn. Each spawn also updates after each objective."\
   ""\
   "Casualty limit: BLUFOR, 250% of its players when safe start ends. This means there can be three respawn waves (300%), but if the 3rd respawn wave receives over 50% casualties, it's a mission fail for BLU."\
   ""\
   "Mission by tanaKa-."
   m_aFactionKeys {
    "BLUFOR"
    "OPFOR"
   }
   m_bShowForAnyFaction 0
  }
  COA_MissionDescriptor "{6AD978D01806B5C4}" {
   m_sTitle "Administration"
   m_sTextData "N/A"
   m_aFactionKeys {
    "BLUFOR"
    "OPFOR"
    "INDFOR"
   }
   m_bShowForAnyFaction 0
  }
 }
 m_iFactionOneRatio 2
